<title>POLAND: Polish minimum T-bill prices fall at tender.</title>
<headline>Polish minimum T-bill prices fall at tender.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Minimum prices of all Polish T-bills fell 0.02 point at today's primary auction on total demand of 455 million zlotys against a one billion zloty offer, the finance ministry said.</p>
<p>The treasury sold a total of 370 million zlotys worth of the bills.</p>
<p>   T-bill	    8-week  13-week  26-week  39-week  52-week</p>
<p>   new min price    --	95.24    90.85     --	83.16</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)    --     (95.26)  (90.87)    --     (83.18)</p>
<p>   new max price    --	95.35    90.89     --	83.40</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)    --     (95.33)  (90.91)    --     (83.40)</p>
<p>   offer		--	300.0    200.0     --	500.0</p>
<p>   bids recorded    --	206.2     39.4     --	209.5</p>
<p>   bids accepted    --	202.7     31.8     --	135.5</p>
<p>   next auction     --	300.0    200.0     --	500.0</p>
<p>NOTE. Offer and all bids in million zlotys.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
